d 'RANGEMATCH': module to perform range and interval-overlap joins between datasets
d
d  rangematch performs a range join between the dataset in memory
d and a using dataset stored on disk or in a named frame. In
d point-in-interval mode it pairs each master observation with
d every using observation whose key variable falls inside the
d master [low, high] interval; in interval-overlap mode, requested
d with overlap(), it pairs master intervals with every overlapping
d using interval. Matching can be restricted within by() groups,
d and options control endpoint closure, floating-point boundary
d tolerance, the policy for missing keys or bounds, retention of
d only the nearest match before or after the key with tie handling,
d treatment of unmatched master and using rows, signed key
d distances, original row identifiers, a ceiling on output size,
d and assertions that required matches exist. Output replaces the
d data in memory or is written to a named frame or a dataset on
d disk, and a dry-run mode reports pair counts without producing
d output. Workspace is managed in Stata frames and pairs are
d generated by Mata binary-search or sweep backends, with no
d external dependencies. The command returns counts of master,
d using, matched, and unmatched rows, missing-bound and missing-key
d diagnostics, optional match-density statistics, and the backend
d used in r(). 
d
d KW: range join
d KW: interval matching
d KW: interval overlap
d KW: merge
d KW: frames
d KW: nearest match
d KW: Mata
d
d Requires: Stata version 16.1
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261030
d
d Author: Timothy P Copeland, Karolinska Institutet
d Support: email timothy.copeland@@ki.se
d
f rangematch.ado
f ../_/_rangematch_mata.ado
f rangematch.sthlp
